// Dungeons and caves (Scott 2026-11-22, D:/LQOnline/dungeons/BRIEF.md: "make it all live to try"). Plain data plus pure
// helpers; the sim reads it as content.dungeons (src/sim/dungeons.js), the map build as the doors to place and check.
//
// Each place is its own zone (kind 'dungeon' or 'cave'), generated by tools/maps/zone_<id>.mjs into
// src/data/maps/<id>.js. Its door on the world is a join pair: a world tile (door.area + door.x, door.y, in that area's
// own tiles; area null = world tiles) that moves a hero into the place's entry, and the entry's exit that puts them back
// on `door.out`. A party (today: one hero) gets its own copy; see CONTRACTS "Dungeons and caves".
//
// Loot per place: `drops[boss]` = the named pool that boss draws from for the killer (pieces the killer's class can use);
// the last boss draws an epic from `rare` (the pool's items are epic since 2026-11-22) and rolls `legendary` (one id, or a
// list: one the killer can use is picked; legend.chance, +legend.step per miss, saved on the hero).
// The Watchtower's bosses also drop their set piece (`setSlot`, src/data/items.js SETS). `daily`: the first clear of each
// real day (the bounty boards' day, world.setDay) leaves a bonus chest by the last boss: gold, glyphs, a gear roll and
// bonus XP worth `xpMinutes` of questing at the hero's level (4 kill XP a minute, BUILDS_2 5.2).
import { BAND_DUNGEONS } from './band_dungeons.js';

export const DUNGEON_RULES = Object.freeze({
  resetSec: 1800,                        // a copy with no hero inside for 30 minutes of sim time resets
  dark: Object.freeze({ dungeon: 0.55, cave: 0.45 }),
  questMinuteKills: 4,                   // questing pace: 4 kill XP a minute at your level (BUILDS_2 5.2)
  label(kind, levels) { return `${kind === 'cave' ? 'Cave' : 'Dungeon'}, levels ${levels[0]} to ${levels[1]}`; },
});

